  "event_seq": 239,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-05). Response-speed (E-04: within SLA) and tariff-change (E-02, E-06: none logged) causes are ruled out. Billing validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 — exactly the surge's first month — changed the high-consumption check to compare raw register values against 12-month m3 history with no unit scaling (E-10), a mechanism that can mis-flag or mis-bill valid reads of either read type. Field route-completion shortfall (E-03: 0.88 vs 0.95 target) cannot explain the dispute buckets: only 320 accounts were actually marked estimated last cycle (E-09), far below the ~1104 the shortfall would imply, so field degradation is too small in magnitude to drive even the ESTIMATED-read bucket (41%, E-01), let alone the larger ACTUAL-read majority (59%, E-01). BV-17's unscaled-comparison defect is the best-supported mechanism for the surge spanning both buckets."
 },
